# Without this file, Git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites line endings
# on checkout. That corrupts the PDF and changes the raw CSVs' bytes, which
# breaks the SHA-256 checksums documented in data/raw/SHA256SUMS.txt. Verified:
# a fresh clone produced a 659,255-byte PDF from a 658,416-byte original.
#
# Later rules win, so the byte-exact rules come last.

# Normalise real text to LF in the index and in the working copy, on every OS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated CSVs and notebooks: text, but always LF so they are stable
# across platforms and diff cleanly.
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.ipynb text eol=lf

# Binary: never transform, never diff as text.
*.pdf    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.joblib binary
*.pkl    binary

# The raw data and its checksums must stay byte-identical, or SHA256SUMS.txt
# stops verifying for anyone who clones. This must be the last word.
data/raw/** -text
